 "response": "Sukukre's budget is now **$1289K**.\n\n**How I worked it out:**\n- Only Finance Office records count. Rumours and estimates from other teams (Operations, Legal, Sales and so on) were ignored.\n- I traced every withdrawal chain to its end. A withdrawal cancels its target only if the withdrawal itself is still in effect after later withdrawals are applied. For example:\n  - #1138 cancels #939, which restores #128. #128 cancels #26, which restores #11, so #8 stays withdrawn.\n  - #1362 cancels #836, which restores #282. #282 cancels #270, so #17 counts.\n  - #1088 cancels #1050, which restores #813. #813 cancels #787, which restores #540. #540 cancels #359, which restores #317, so #298 stays withdrawn.\n- Three changes were withdrawn and then restored, so they count: #1217 (+$554K), #1302 (\u2212$514K) and #653 (+$467K).\n- Starting from the $2130K set in #0001, I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease still in effect, in order. That gives $1289K after the last change (#1598, +$70K).\n\nANSWER: $1289K",
